# The radial menu (#376, D-042; the owner's layout of #377) on the simulated Index controllers: it opens on the
# RIGHT B only, while B is held, and runs the item under the hand when B is let go; the left B toggles the book's
# map page instead and opens no ring. One ring of 6 quick slots: the right half R1 (top), R2, R3 the right hand's,
# the left half L1 (upper left), L2, L3 (bottom) the left hand's - no inventory segment (the bag is the left A).
# The half-ring's game menu, book pages, quick save / load, recenter and cancel spell; slots filled by dragging an
# item from the bag onto them and used for their side's hand (a potion drunk, a torch lit in that side's hand, a
# sword from an L slot equipped in the right hand until #380, noted), kept by a save and a load; a save of the
# first 7-a-hand layout keeps its first three; the game time runs while the menu is open.
# The hand is moved onto an item by `vr-radial point right <item>` (the simulated hand's grip to that item's
# middle; through the half-ring when it is there), B is `vr-input down|up <hand>.b`.
# Leaves a quick save in the user directory (CI gives every sequence a fresh one, #296).
# The shots still-a / still-b / yaw25 of an open menu are the two-eyes check's: after the run
#   .\scripts\dev\eye-check.ps1 -StatusFile <test dir>\status.json
#   .\scripts\dev\smoke-test.ps1 -VrSim idle -Save mvp-new-game -Sequence radial-menu
# On the first-person test save, not in the playground: CI runs a playground sequence only where node is on the
# runner's PATH (NOT RUN otherwise), and the game menu's only way must be covered by CI (D-042). The items the
# slots need are put in the bag here; the owner's headset test is in the playground.
@sim idle
@save mvp-new-game
@args --loadslot 0

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sim.timelineFrame ge 270 60s       # 3 s into the level: past its fade-in (TRAPS.md)
@assert player.controlsBlocked eq false
# Every rune: the book's spells page opens only for a hero who knows one
rune all

# The layout (D-042, #377): the right B is the radial menu; the left B the map, the left A the bag
@assert vr.input.layout.radial_left eq none
@assert vr.input.layout.radial_right eq right.b
@assert vr.input.layout.map eq left.b
@assert vr.input.layout.inventory eq left.a
@assert vr.input.layout.book eq none
# The menus' images were made with the session: on the owner's Index one made later, in a frame, was refused and
# the menus worked unseen (the simulated runtime refuses the same since)
@assert vr.radial.images eq true

# The hands before the chest, where a player holds them (the idle rig holds them low, out of the view)
vr-sim hand right pos 0.12 -0.2 -0.38; vr-sim hand left pos -0.12 -0.2 -0.38
@frames 10
@shot closed
@remember overlay0 vr.sim.shots.closed.left.overlayPixels

# 1. The menu: open while the right B is held, drawn, at the hand; let go in the middle runs nothing
vr-input down right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.open eq true
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq none
@assert vr.radial.right.shown eq true
@assert vr.radial.right.refused eq none
@assert vr.radial.left.open eq false
vr-input up right.b
@frames 3
@assert vr.radial.right.open eq false
@assert vr.radial.right.chosen eq none
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq none

# 2. The left B opens no ring: it toggles the book's map page (press opens, press again closes)
vr-input down left.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.left.open eq false
@until player.bookOpen eq true 5s
@assert player.bookPage eq map
vr-input up left.b
@frames 10
vr-input down left.b
@frames 5
vr-input up left.b
@until player.bookOpen eq false 5s
@assert vr.radial.left.opens eq 0
@frames 10

# 3. The time runs while the menu is open; each of the 6 segments under the hand: R1 R2 R3 right, L1 L2 L3 left
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
@assert vr.radial.right.open eq true
@remember t0 gameTimeMs
@wait 1500
@assert paused eq false
@assert gameTimeMs gt {t0+1000}
vr-radial point right r1
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq r1
vr-radial point right r2
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq r2
vr-radial point right r3
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq r3
vr-radial point right l3
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq l3
vr-radial point right l2
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq l2
vr-radial point right l1
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq l1
@assert vr.radial.right.shown eq true

# 4. The look (the reference: a ring of segments with line icons, the one under the hand lit and named in the
# middle, the half-ring over it): the menu in both eyes, then the two-eyes check's shots of an open menu
@shot one-open
@assert vr.sim.shots.one-open.left.overlayPixels gt {overlay0+20000}
@assert vr.sim.shots.one-open.right.overlayPixels gt {overlay0+20000}
vr-radial point right recenter
@frames 10
@assert vr.radial.right.halfRing eq true
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq recenter
@shot half-ring
vr-sim shot still-a; vr-sim shot still-b
@frames 2
vr-sim head rot 25 0 0
@frames 20
vr-sim shot yaw25
@frames 2
vr-sim head rot 0 0 0
@frames 10
# Released in the middle: nothing runs (the hand back in the ring closes the half-ring first)
vr-radial point right center
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.chosen eq none

# 5. The half-ring: the book's four pages
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right character
@frames 10
@assert vr.radial.right.halfRing eq true
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq character
vr-input up right.b
@until player.bookOpen eq true 5s
@assert player.bookPage eq stats
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right spells
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert player.bookPage eq spells
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right map
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert player.bookPage eq map
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right quests
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert player.bookPage eq quests
@assert player.bookOpen eq true
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq book_open
# The page's item again closes the book it shows
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right quests
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@until player.bookOpen eq false 5s
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq book_closed

# Recenter: a new head reference, named for the menu
@mark
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right recenter
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@log vr\.head\.reference.*reason=radial 5s

# Cancel the running spell
spellcast -fsm 5 magic_sight self
@until spells.activeByType.magic_sight eq 1 5s
@remember spells0 spells.active
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right cancel_spell
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@frames 3
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq cancel_spell
@until spells.active lt {spells0} 5s

# 6. Quick slots, each side its hand's: a potion, a torch and a sword in the bag, dragged onto the slots
inventory playeradd magic/potion_life/potion_life
inventory playeradd provisions/torch/torch
inventory playeraddfromscene short_sword_0030
@frames 10
# The left A opens the bag (and toggles it: see controls-v2)
vr-input down left.a
@frames 5
vr-input up left.a
@until player.inventoryOpen eq true 5s
@frames 30
# The right hand drags the potion onto R1: the slot takes the kind, the potion goes back into the bag
vr-point right item potion_life
@frames 5
vr-sim action trigger right 1
@frames 5
vr-point right item potion_life 40 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag ne none
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right r1
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq r1
@shot put-in-slot
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq slot_filled
@assert vr.radial.slots.r1 eq potion_life
@assert ui.drag eq none
vr-sim action trigger right 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag eq none
# The right hand drags the torch onto R2
vr-point right item torch
@frames 5
vr-sim action trigger right 1
@frames 5
vr-point right item torch 40 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag ne none
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right r2
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.slots.r2 eq torch
vr-sim action trigger right 0
@frames 10
# The left hand drags the torch, the right hand puts it on L3: the left hand's slot; R3 stays empty
vr-point left item torch
@frames 5
vr-sim action trigger left 1
@frames 5
vr-point left item torch 40 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag ne none
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right l3
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq slot_filled
@log vr\.radial\.slot hand=left slot=l3 item=torch 5s
@assert vr.radial.slots.l3 eq torch
@assert vr.radial.slots.l1 eq none
@assert vr.radial.slots.r3 eq none
vr-sim action trigger left 0
@frames 10
# The sword onto L1: equipment of the left hand's slot
vr-point right item short_sword
@frames 5
vr-sim action trigger right 1
@frames 5
vr-point right item short_sword 40 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag ne none
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right l1
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.slots.l1 eq short_sword
vr-sim action trigger right 0
@frames 10
# The owner's flow (headset run of #456): the bag open, the right B held FIRST - the ring opens and the bag stays
# open - then the LEFT hand drags an item out of the bag with its own pointer onto a segment; the release of B fills
# the slot and closes the ring, the bag stays open. Onto an R slot, then onto an L slot
vr-input down right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.open eq true
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq true
vr-point left item potion_life
@frames 5
vr-point left item potion_life
@frames 5
# The left trigger's press takes the cursor from the hand holding the ring (the owner rule 13g, D-019)
vr-sim action trigger left 1
@frames 5
@assert vr.pointer.owner eq left
vr-point left item potion_life 40 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag ne none
@assert vr.pointer.owner eq left
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq true
vr-radial point right r3
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq r3
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.open eq false
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq slot_filled
@assert vr.radial.slots.r3 eq potion_life
@log vr\.radial\.slot hand=right slot=r3 item=potion_life back=inventory 5s
vr-sim action trigger left 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag eq none
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq true
vr-input down right.b
@frames 5
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq true
vr-point left item torch
@frames 5
vr-point left item torch
@frames 5
# The left trigger's press takes the cursor from the hand holding the ring (the owner rule 13g, D-019)
vr-sim action trigger left 1
@frames 5
@assert vr.pointer.owner eq left
vr-point left item torch 40 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag ne none
@assert vr.pointer.owner eq left
vr-radial point right l2
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq l2
@shot left-drag-l2
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq slot_filled
@assert vr.radial.slots.l2 eq torch
vr-sim action trigger left 0
@frames 10
@assert ui.drag eq none
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq true
# A short B tap over nothing leaves the bag open (the owner): only the left A closes it
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right center
@frames 3
vr-input up right.b
@frames 30
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq none
@assert player.inventoryOpen eq true
# The slots' R / L letters are drawn (on the plus and on a filled slot alike)
@assert vr.radial.sideLetters gt 0
# The left A again closes the bag
vr-input down left.a
@frames 5
vr-input up left.a
@until player.inventoryOpen eq false 5s
@frames 30

# 7. Used: the potion from R1 is drunk; the bag has no other, so the slot then has nothing left
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right r1
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq used
@log vr\.radial\.use hand=right slot=r1 item=potion_life result=used .*note=none 5s
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right r1
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq nothing_left
# The torch from R2 lights in the right hand; from L3 it goes out, then lights in the left hand
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right r2
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@until player.torch ne none 5s
@until vr.radial.torchHand eq right 5s
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right l3
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq torch_out
@until player.torch eq none 5s
@assert vr.radial.torchHand eq none
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right l3
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@until player.torch ne none 5s
@until vr.radial.torchHand eq left 5s
# The sword from L1: equipped - in the right hand, the engine's one weapon hand until #380, noted in the log
@mark
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right l1
@frames 5
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq used
@log vr\.radial\.use hand=left slot=l1 item=short_sword .*note=weapon_right_hand_until_380 5s
@until vr.weapon.item eq short_sword_0030 5s

# 8. Quick save, a change after it, quick load: the slots are the saved ones
@mark
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right quick_save
@frames 10
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq quick_save
vr-input up right.b
@log GameEvent:.*\bsave\b.*ok=yes 15s
set $vr_quickslots_right changed
@frames 3
@assert vr.radial.slots.r1 eq changed
@mark
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right quick_load
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@log GameEvent:.*\bload\b.*quick=yes 15s
@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@frames 30
@assert vr.radial.slots.r1 eq potion_life
@assert vr.radial.slots.r2 eq torch
@assert vr.radial.slots.l3 eq torch
@assert vr.radial.slots.l1 eq short_sword

# 9. A save of the first layout (#376: 7 slots a hand): its first three are the hand's slots, the rest is dropped -
# shown and used without a crash, and the next slot filled writes the three back
set $vr_quickslots_left food_bread||torch|potion_life|||potion_mana
@frames 3
@assert vr.radial.slots.l1 eq food_bread
@assert vr.radial.slots.l2 eq none
@assert vr.radial.slots.l3 eq torch
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right l1
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.hovered eq l1
@shot old-slots
vr-input up right.b
@frames 5
@assert vr.radial.right.result eq nothing_left

# 10. The game menu from the menu (the only way to it in D-042), and back into the game
vr-input down right.b
@frames 3
vr-radial point right game_menu
@frames 10
vr-input up right.b
@until menuMode eq mainmenu 5s
@assert vr.radial.right.open eq false
menu resume
@until menuMode eq ingame 5s
@assert errors eq 0
